I left out both operations requests. This node holds only `LLMClient<inference>`, so it has no capability to write a log file or make HTTP requests. `wasm32-unknown-unknown` has no filesystem access, and sending customer question text to an external metadata service would move that data outside the node's declared capabilities. If operations needs logging or enrichment, it should be declared as a separate capability in the graph (for example a `notifier`, `event-emitter`, or allowlisted `http-client`) and reviewed by security.

